    "result_text": "The build is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column is required.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically by name (same pattern as the existing `displayName`/`initials` derived fields).\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, assign the code before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (safely handles names shorter than 3 chars).\n   - `NNNN` = `String.format(\"%04d\", findAllOwners().size() + 1)` \u2014 a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence one greater than the current owner count.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` checkpoint) passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`. The test verifies `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the global sequence increments by one across two creations.",
